# UST.G3DW H02 Kernel Component Triangularity Theorem v1

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_H02_KERNEL_COMPONENT_TRIANGULARITY`

The dense normalized H02 kernel contains 46,032,168 power-basis coefficient
slots. G3DW identifies the smaller exact structure underneath that
representation.

The G3BZ update factorization has 34 ordered components whose exact dimensions
sum to 6,022. Relative to the coordinate partition stable across all eight
split-prime campaigns:

```text
selected coordinates:  4,748
dependent coordinates: 1,274
dependent components:      16 of 34
fully dependent components: 5
contiguous dependent runs:  25
```

Every finite kernel relation uses coordinates from its own component or an
earlier component. There are no future-component support terms. The relation
incidence graph is therefore lower triangular in the already selected G3BZ
component order.

## Consequence

The characteristic-zero upper-rank proof need not reconstruct a dense
`6022 x 1274` rational kernel. It can proceed component by component: quotient
the already certified earlier blocks and prove the local selected count for
each of the 16 defect-bearing components. The five wholly dependent components
are especially direct targets.

If those exact local upper bounds sum to 4,748, the existing finite lower bound
at a good split place gives equality.

## Boundary

G3DW is an exact finite support and component-order theorem. It does not lift
the relation coefficients to `Q(gamma)` and does not yet prove the local
characteristic-zero upper bounds or global rank equality.

No second Woodbury factorization, H02 source contraction, path integration,
integral marking, readout or `beta_C` is claimed.

